<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ziębice</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Münsterberg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ziębice (German Münsterberg) is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-silesia">Lower Silesia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wroclaw">Wrocław</a>. From 1322 it was the seat of a Piast duchy and later passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-of-podebrady">George of Poděbrady</a>, whose sons held it as dukes of Münsterberg, and from 1654 to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-auersperg">Auersperg family</a>. Prussian from 1742, it became part of Poland in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ziebice.jpg" alt="Ziębice" width="320" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacek Halicki · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2019_Ratusz_w_Zi%C4%99bicach_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
